    "name": "1358",
    "category": "bacterial",
    "description": "1358. NBRC 1356.",
    "medium_type": "complex",
    "physical_state": "liquid",
    "high_metal": false,
    "high_ree": false,
    "target_organism_names": [],
    "organism_culture_type": "",
    "organism_ids": [],
    "ingredient_names": [
      "Mineral base 1*500mlMineral base 2**500mlMgCl2\u00b76H2O0.2gBacto Yeast Extract (Difco)0.02gCoenzyme M0.014gVitamin solution***5mlTrace element solution****10mlMethanol2mlSodium formate3.4gSodium acetate0.16gFeS slurry solution*****2mlNa2S\u00b79H2O0.12gMix mineral base 1 with mineral base 2 in 1:1 proportion in tightly closed vessels under a N2atmosphere. Separately autoclave concentrated Bacto Yeast Extract, coenzyme M, sodium acetate, Na2S\u00b79H2O and FeS solution under a N2atmosphere in tightly closed vessels. Add the autoclaved concentrated solutions, and filter-sterile concentrated MgCl2\u00b76H2O, vitamin solution, trace element solution, methanol and sodium formate solution. After re-exchanging with N2, add 1 drop of filter-sterile 10% sodium dithionaite solution in 1 M NaHCO3by syringe. Final pH of the complete medium should be 9.*Mineral base 1Na2CO3185gNaHCO335gNaCl16gK2HPO41gDistilled water1LMix ingredients and autoclave under a N2atmosphere. Because some precipitate appears on the bottom for 1 day after autoclaving, use only supernatant for making the medium. Final pH should be 10.**Mineral base 2NaCl240gNH4Cl0.5gK2HPO42.5gKCl5gDistilled water1LMix ingredients and autoclave under a N2atmosphere. Final pH should be 7.3.***Vitamin solutionBiotin2mgFolic acid2mgPyridoxine-HCl10mgThiamine-HCl5mgRiboflavin5mgNicotinic acid5mgCa-pantothenate5mgp-Aminobenzoic acid1mgVitamin B120.01mgDistilled water1L****Trace elements solutionNitrilotriacetic acid (NTA)12.8gFeCl3\u00b76H2O1.35gMnCl2\u00b74H2O0.1gCoCl2\u00b76H2O0.024gCaCl2\u00b72H2O0.1gZnCl20.1gCuCl2\u00b72H2O0.025gH3BO30.01gNa2MoO4\u00b72H2O0.024gNaCl1gNiCl2\u00b76H2O0.12gNa2SeO40.004gNa2WO40.004gDistilled water1LFirst dissolve nitrilotriacetic acid and adjust pH to 6.5 with NaOH, and then add minerals. Final pH 7.0.*****FeS slurry solutionMix 0.5 M FeSO4\u00b77H2O and 0.5 M Na2S\u00b79H2O solutions, wash with pure water several times, finally resuspend the FeS precipitate as 20% solution and autoclave (110\u00b0C, 30 min) under a N2atmosphere."
    ],
