      "NaCl30gK2HPO40.14gCaCl2\u00b72H2O0.14gNH4Cl0.25gMgSO4\u00b77H2O3.4gMgCl2\u00b76H2O4.2gKCl0.33gFe(NH4)2(SO4)2\u00b76H2O0.01gBacto Yeast Extract (Difco)1gTrace elements solution*10mlVitamin solution**2mlNaHCO32.5gSulfur (powder)3gResazurin1mgNa2S\u00b79H2O0.5gDistilled water1LMix ingredients except for vitamin solution, sulfur, and Na2S\u00b79H2O. Dispense the medium into suitable culture vessels under a stream of N2/CO2(80/20), seal with butyl rubber stoppers, and autoclave at 121\u00b0C for 15 min. Separately neutralize and autoclave Na2S\u00b79H2O (5% solution) under N2atmosphere. Sterilize vitamin solution by filtration. Sulfur is sterilized separately by autoclaving for 60 min at 105\u00b0C on each of 3 successive days. Prior to inoculation, aseptically and anaerobically add vitamin, sulfur, and Na2S\u00b79H2O. Final pH is 6.8.*Trace elements solutionNitrilotriacetic acid (NTA)12.8gFeCl3\u00b76H2O1.35gMnCl2\u00b74H2O0.1gCoCl2\u00b76H2O0.024gCaCl2\u00b72H2O0.1gZnCl20.1gCuCl2\u00b72H2O0.025gH3BO30.01gNa2MoO4\u00b72H2O0.024gNaCl1gNiCl2\u00b76H2O0.12gNa2SeO40.8mgNa2WO40.8mgKAl(SO4)2\u00b712H2O4mgDistilled water1LFirst dissolve nitrilotriacetic acid and adjust pH to 6.5 with NaOH, and then add minerals. Final pH is 7.0.**Vitamin solutionBiotin2mgFolic acid2mgPyridoxine-HCl10mgThiamine-HCl5mgRiboflavin5mgNicotinic acid5mgCa-pantothenate5mgp-Aminobenzoic acid1mgVitamin B120.01mgDistilled water1L"
